      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The bayou was first called 'Riviere D'Erbane' and later took its name from a French artillery battery on the west bank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayou_La_Batre%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The local chamber of commerce has described the city as the 'Seafood Capital of Alabama' for packaging seafood from hundreds of fishing boats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
